Run the FlClash core as a standalone daemon.

The FlClash branch is embedded in the FlClash app, whose own Go glue starts the
inbound listeners and the TUN device; ApplyConfig therefore skips both. Upstream
mihomo (ab405ba, the closest Alpha commit) calls them here. Restoring the two calls
makes 'mixed-port' and 'tun' in the -f profile take effect on start and reload.
Nothing else in the core changes.

diff --git a/hub/executor/executor.go b/hub/executor/executor.go
index dc7c66b..ad7c079 100644
--- a/hub/executor/executor.go
+++ b/hub/executor/executor.go
@@ -104,8 +104,8 @@ func ApplyConfig(cfg *config.Config, force bool) {
 	updateGeneral(cfg.General, true)
 	updateDNS(cfg.DNS, cfg.General.IPv6)
 	updateNTP(cfg.NTP) // initialize NTP after DNS because an NTP server may be a hostname.
-	//updateListeners(cfg.General, cfg.Listeners, force)
-	//updateTun(cfg.General) // tun should not care "force"
+	updateListeners(cfg.General, cfg.Listeners, force)
+	updateTun(cfg.General) // tun should not care "force"
 	updateIPTables(cfg)
 	updateTunnels(cfg.Tunnels)
 
